      "writtenOn": "2021-07-13T07:18:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the old way of doing it. While it would \"work\", we have a newer framework that will let us test, let apps opt-in, give us free logging : compat @ChangeId.\n\nGuide is at https://g3doc.corp.google.com/wireless/android/art/compat/g3doc/dev/compat-framework.md?cl\u003dhead\n\nIn a nutshell, what you\u0027d do is\n• Import android.compat.annotation.ChangeId and other annotations you\n  need from that package\n• Add a long equal to the buganizer bug ID annotated with @ChangeId, e.g. :\n  /**\n   * When enabled, apps targetting \u003c Android 12 are considered legacy for\n   * the NSD native daemon.\n   * The platform will only keep the daemon running as long as there are\n   * any legacy apps connected.\n   */\n  @ChangeId\n  @EnabledSince(targetSdkVersion\u003dandroid.os.Build.VERSION_CODES.S)\n  private static final long RUN_NATIVE_NSD_ONLY_IF_LEGACY_APPS \u003d 12345L;\n• Gate on the change, e.g. :\n  if (CompatChanges.isChangeEnabled(RUN_NATIVE...)) {\n    // do the new thing\n  } else {\n    // do the old thing\n  }\n• You can also have a CTS for this. Using @ChangeId will simplify writing\n  the test because you can simulate either behavior rather than having to\n  write an app with target S and one with target R.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 504,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 505,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "5468fac78ab662d78aa522835cf14f1ff4d6015b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
